fix(media-controls): implement MPRIS Shuffle and LoopStatus

qbz-media-controls published both properties but the handlers were stubs:
`Shuffle` always read false, `LoopStatus` always `None`, and both setters
returned Ok without doing anything. With `CanControl=true` a KDE/GNOME
widget shows the buttons, swallows the clicks and displays a state that
never matches the queue. Affects the desktop and qbzd alike, since they
share the crate.

Everything below the crate already existed: QbzCore has set_shuffle and
set_repeat_mode, QueueState carries shuffle/repeat, RepeatMode maps 1:1
onto LoopStatus (Off/All/One -> None/Playlist/Track), and the core emits
ShuffleChanged / RepeatModeChanged on the bus.

qbz-media-controls
  LoopMode + MediaEvent::{SetShuffle, SetLoop}; MediaIntegration gains
  set_shuffle / set_loop with default no-ops (SMTC and MediaRemote have no
  such property). The MPRIS backend keeps both in State, answers the getters
  from it, emits PropertiesChanged on push and forwards writes as events.

qbzd
  Seeds both from get_queue_state, follows ShuffleChanged /
  RepeatModeChanged on the bus, and applies writes via the core's async
  setters spawned off the D-Bus thread.

qbz-qt (desktop)
  Not wired, and deliberately so. The desktop this patch first covered is
  gone — the Qt port replaced `crates/qbz` wholesale — and an MPRIS write
  carries a TARGET where the only Qt entry points are the toggle/cycle steps
  (`transport_toggle_shuffle`, `transport_cycle_repeat`), which flip the
  wrong way whenever the target already matches. Targeted setters behind the
  Qt QConnect gate are desktop work, not a rebase, so `dispatch` drops both
  events under a named arm rather than by accident. The getters still report
  the queue, and the daemon — the only binary this tree ships — applies them.

Verified: `cargo check --locked` on qbz-media-controls and qbzd. The desktop
crate was not compiled locally.

Taken from the fork branch b0bbywan/qbz:bugfix/external/mpris-shuffle-loop
(267ee043), written against upstream pre-release at 82fea625 and rebased
onto 353ed7ff daemon-side only. Drops once upstream merges it.

